nodes.prompt:
Implement this spec in the repo. Then report what you changed, file by file.

SPEC:
{spec}

Original task for context:
{input}

Review this implementation as an adversarial reviewer. You did not write it.

SPEC:
{spec}

AUTHOR'S REPORT:
{build}

Read the actual files on disk — do not trust the report. Find real defects only: correctness bugs, unhandled inputs, security issues, spec violations, needless complexity. For each: file:line, why it breaks, concrete fix. If you find nothing real, say so — do not manufacture findings.

You are the judge. Neither of the two agents below may overrule you, and you wrote neither artifact.

SPEC:
{spec}

BUILD (codex):
{build}

REVIEW (agy):
{review}

For each review finding decide: VALID (fix now) / MINOR (log it) / WRONG (reviewer erred — say why). Then give the verdict: SHIP or BLOCK, and if BLOCK, the exact remaining work as a numbered list.
